@mainpage TVPaint Animation SDK Documentation



@section sec_naming  About the naming of things...

Functions starting with "PI_" are used for calls to a plugin from TVPaint. These are the only exported functions from the shared library.

Other things starting with "PI" are used by the plugin.

Things (structs, functions, constants, etc...) starting with "TV" are used for calls to TVPaint from a plugin.

This is a work in progress, not everything follows this guideline, yet.

Enumerators are prefixed with either 'k' or 'b'.\n
'k' means they are constants.\n
'b' means they are bits, you can OR them together to form a set of flags.\n
In a few cases, an enumeration has both 'k' and 'b' enumerators, this means you have to choose one of the 'k's, and may OR it together with some of the 'b's.


@section sec_timer  About timers...

When you get a timer value, it is the number of milliseconds ellapsed from some arbitrary start time.
You should only use differences of two such values.



@ref  calling_sequence
*/



